2. Max how many columns we can create clustering in bigquery
In BigQuery, you can specify up to 4 clustering columns for a table.
can use clustering on a standalone table (non-partitioned) or combine clustering with partitioning. In a partitioned table, clustering is maintained within each partition.

2. What is Partitioning, Clustering & Sharding in BQ.
Partitioning is like dividing table into smaller partitions for better performance. same as PARTITION BY
Clustering is sorting the data based on one or more columns in table, so based on date, country, status will cluster. same as ORDER BY
Sharding is breaking if data into smaller pieces.

